WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.906 --> 00:00:11.707
One day some scientists looked around and saw that the rivers were very dirty, and that there were

2
00:00:11.747 --> 00:00:12.688
less fish to catch.

3
00:00:13.888 --> 00:00:19.189
They also noticed that there were fewer birds and dragonflies, and that the trees were starting to die.

4
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.731
They couldn't find what was causing the problem.

5
00:00:24.731 --> 00:00:27.612
But they noticed something else was missing—the beaver.

6
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:33.484
So scientists decided to study how beavers live so that they can bring them back to the rivers.

7
00:00:37.347 --> 00:00:40.370
Wherever beavers live, they make big changes to nature.

8
00:00:41.651 --> 00:00:45.133
In fact, the only creatures who affect nature more are humans!

9
00:00:46.895 --> 00:00:53.180
However, unlike humans, the changes that beavers make are good for the other animals and plants around them.

10
00:00:54.928 --> 00:00:58.972
Once a beaver finds an empty spot on a stream or river, it builds a dam.

11
00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:04.696
As soon as the dam is built, the land upstream begins to fill with water.

12
00:01:05.597 --> 00:01:08.940
The extra water changes the land behind the dam into a wetland.

13
00:01:11.842 --> 00:01:17.126
A wetland is a wide area of mud and water, and wetlands are very important habitats.

14
00:01:18.387 --> 00:01:23.812
In fact, over half of North America's endangered species need wetlands to survive.

15
00:01:25.368 --> 00:01:30.290
Once a beaver makes its dam, it takes care to make sure the water level around the dam

16
00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:30.990
stays high.

17
00:01:34.651 --> 00:01:38.312
The beaver does this to protect its home, but it also protects nature.

18
00:01:39.993 --> 00:01:43.574
The dam slows down a river, which helps make the water cleaner.

19
00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:49.776
And instead of the river carrying good soil away to the ocean, the dam keeps the soil in

20
00:01:49.796 --> 00:01:50.356
the forest.

21
00:01:54.364 --> 00:01:59.688
Even though beavers cut down trees to make their dams, they actually help the trees to grow.

22
00:01:59.708 --> 00:02:05.632
A beaver's favorite trees for eating and building are cottonwoods and aspens.

23
00:02:06.313 --> 00:02:09.595
Both of these trees make hundreds of baby trees every year.

24
00:02:10.416 --> 00:02:17.120
However, if all the baby trees lived, they would eventually get too crowded, and they all would die.

25
00:02:17.881 --> 00:02:22.084
But when the beaver takes out some of the trees, it gives the rest more room to grow.

26
00:02:22.764 --> 00:02:24.466
This helps keep the forests healthy.

27
00:02:26.047 --> 00:02:29.950
Beavers eat only plants, and this makes its other animal friends happy.

28
00:02:31.111 --> 00:02:39.998
The wetland created by a beaver dam gives otter, mink, muskrats, deer, bears, dragonflies, turtles, frogs, and ducks—

29
00:02:40.519 --> 00:02:43.441
and lots of other birds—a place to grow and hunt.

30
00:02:44.942 --> 00:02:51.207
The reason scientists couldn't find fish or dragonflies or birds is that the beavers weren't there building their

31
00:02:51.227 --> 00:02:59.633
dams. Even though beavers keep the rivers clean, the trees growing, and the other animals alive, many people

32
00:02:59.673 --> 00:03:00.813
get angry with beavers.

33
00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:06.857
When dams make wetlands, sometimes they ruin a farmer's field or flood a road.

34
00:03:08.558 --> 00:03:11.500
Some dams make it hard for fish to travel in streams.

35
00:03:12.521 --> 00:03:17.785
But when people try to trap beavers to take them away, a new beaver always moves in.

36
00:03:18.945 --> 00:03:24.341
So scientists are studying ways to help beavers and humans live together so we can all make changes

37
00:03:24.742 --> 00:03:26.083
that will be good for nature.
